<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 58 0 R
/T ( A portfolio application can produce numerically correct results while failing as a product. It may preserve stale analysis after the user changes an input, accept an invalid symbol, present an infeasible allocation, or conceal that the benchmark series is unavailable. These failures are especially serious in a financial context because a plausible interface can cause the user to trust an output that no longer corresponds to the visible conditions. Finfolio 2.0 therefore required a quality process that covered behavior and state, not only isolated formulas.)
/E ( A portfolio application can produce numerically correct results while failing as a product. It may preserve stale analysis after the user changes an input, accept an invalid symbol, present an infeasible allocation, or conceal that the benchmark series is unavailable. These failures are especially serious in a financial context because a plausible interface can cause the user to trust an output that no longer corresponds to the visible conditions. Finfolio 2.0 therefore required a quality process that covered behavior and state, not only isolated formulas.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
104 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 58 0 R
/T ( As Product Manager and Flow and Testing Lead, I converted the target-user problem and financial specifications into user journeys, validation rules, acceptance scenarios, bug records, and release checks. I owned the happy path from portfolio entry to decision recording, alternative paths involving source or benchmark fallback, and error paths involving invalid data or constraints. I also reviewed whether important methodology and limitation statements remained visible beside the outputs they qualify.)
/E ( As Product Manager and Flow and Testing Lead, I converted the target-user problem and financial specifications into user journeys, validation rules, acceptance scenarios, bug records, and release checks. I owned the happy path from portfolio entry to decision recording, alternative paths involving source or benchmark fallback, and error paths involving invalid data or constraints. I also reviewed whether important methodology and limitation statements remained visible beside the outputs they qualify.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [1]
>>
