135 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 61 0 R
/E ( The bug log records symptom, severity, affected flow, expected behavior, actual behavior, cause, owner, correction, and regression evidence. This structure prevented a defect from being closed merely because the interface appeared improved in one manual attempt. A fix was accepted only when the original trigger was repeated and the related automated or production check passed.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
136 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 61 0 R
/E ( Examples included a scheduled refresh that downloaded data successfully but failed while publishing a missing branch, a recent cache timestamp that concealed an old market session, a result remaining visible after an input change, and allocation caps that could not sum to 100%. Each issue connected product behavior with a technical correction. The freshness defect, for example, led to a separate latest-session check and regression tests that distinguish download time from market recency.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
137 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 61 0 R
/E ( Figure 3 shows how the resulting application state keeps data timing, limitations, headline output, and contribution controls visible together.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [4]
>>
