147 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 62 0 R
/E ( During Weeks 1 and 2, I consolidated candidate problems, instructor feedback, and the selected MVP into an observable sequence. The user need was narrowed to understanding return and risk across a multi-asset portfolio and comparing a constrained alternative. Features such as brokerage execution and personalized automated advice were kept outside the core path because they were not necessary to demonstrate the analytical value.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
148 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 62 0 R
/E ( In Week 3, the sequence became a validation matrix. Every critical input received a rule, expected response, and downstream consequence. A missing or invalid value had to block the affected calculation, while an acceptable fallback had to remain visible. This matrix created a bridge between the Data Lead's dictionary and the Lead Developer's input handlers and API errors.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
149 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 62 0 R
/E (3.1 Requirement synthesis and validation matrix)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
150 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 62 0 R
/E ( Week 5 introduced integrated acceptance scenarios covering a valid multi-asset portfolio, invalid amounts, benchmark gaps, reconciliation, feasible and infeasible optimization, before-and-after consistency, and prohibited advice-like language. Each case recorded the input, action, expected visible result, and evidence. During Week 6, these cases were executed against the first working build, and deviations were recorded in the bug log rather than summarized as an unsupported pass percentage.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
151 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 62 0 R
/E ( The final Week 7 audit reviewed the automated suites, representative desktop and mobile routes, data freshness, optimization, simulation, and production deployment. On 23 October 2026, the repository recorded 50 JavaScript and 35 Python tests passing. The audit also checked a provider-backed FPT, HPG, and GLD portfolio, VN30 comparison, optimization under 80% instrument and 60% commodity limits, and a seeded 2,000-path simulation. Figure 4 illustrates the form in which simulation limitations remain adjacent to the model output.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
