<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 64 0 R
/E ( Testing was primarily internal and did not include a large external user-acceptance sample. The test suite verifies defined behavior but cannot prove that all retail investors understand the explanations. Provider outages and revisions can be handled transparently but cannot be eliminated by application testing. Production checks also depend on representative routes and viewports rather than every possible browser and device combination.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
168 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 64 0 R
/E ( The main lesson was the difference between a plausible requirement and a verifiable result. A requirement becomes useful when it has a trigger, expected visible behavior, actual observation, and regression check. Numerical identities are particularly valuable because they remain stable when market values change. The process also showed that limitations should be tested as content: an advanced metric without its assumption can be a product defect even when the number is calculated correctly.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
