/Title (A portfolio application can produce numerically correct results while failing as a product. It may preserve stale analysis after the user changes an input, accept an invalid symbol, present an infeasible allocation, or conceal that the benchmark series is unavailable. These failures are especially serious in a financial context because a plausible interface can cause the user to trust an output that no longer corresponds to the visible conditions. Finfolio 2.0 therefore required a quality process that covered behavior and state, not only isolated formulas.)
